      "body": "## Overview\n\nSynchronize KV transfer engine IDs across PCP ranks before the existing PP broadcast. This draft addresses a multi-node startup failure observed with PP2/PCP8/TP2; hardware validation is pending.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Workers in a TP/PCP/PP model-parallel instance converge on the ID from TP0/PCP0/PP0 before connector construction.\n- PCP=1 retains the existing broadcast path, and synchronization does not cross DP engine boundaries.\n- No new unit tests are included. This remains a draft until the distributed serving reproducer is validated.\n\n## Validation\n\nPending validation.\n\n## Details\n\nEach node can construct its own KV transfer configuration. With PP2/PCP8/TP2 on four 8-device nodes, initial IDs A/B/C/D remain A/B/A/B after the existing TP and PP broadcasts. A connector that validates worker identities, such as Ascend Mooncake V2, rejects this metadata before serving starts.\n\nBroadcasting across PCP between TP and PP instead gives A/B/C/D -> A/A/C/C -> A/A/A/A. This selects the same model-parallel origin without generating a new ID or broadcasting across DP. The additional object collective runs only during connector initialization when PCP>1, not in the token-generation loop.\n\nDuplicate-work check: searched open PRs for `_sync_engine_id_across_tp`, PCP engine IDs, and engine-ID synchronization. No matching PCP synchronization fix was found. #39276 addresses global versus local DP suffixes and MoRIIO behavior; #43366 addresses NIXL PP support. Neither changes this PCP broadcast. Related Ascend workarounds: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/19398 and https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/19399.\n\nAI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used to prepare the code and this description. Human review and end-to-end validation remain pending before this draft is marked ready.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
